{
    "background_story": "Cuddles, the colorful parrot, was known for her loquacious nature. She would often regale her owner, Mrs. Jenkins, with lengthy tales of her adventures in the aviary. Cuddles' stories would meander through topics, from the intricacies of seed selection to the drama of bird social politics. Her discursiveness was both charming and exhausting, as she would ramble on for hours, barely pausing for breath. Despite this, Mrs. Jenkins adored Cuddles' chatty nature, finding herself enthralled by the parrot's vivid descriptions and witty observations. Cuddles' ability to weave complex narratives had a way of making even the most mundane events seem fascinating, earning her the title of 'Resident Storyteller' among the Jenkins' household.",
